IMPORT prelude

-- Diplomatic and Consular Officers (Oaths and Fees) Act 1968 (Singapore) -- oaths, affidavits and notarial acts done before a
-- Singapore diplomatic or consular officer abroad (s 3), proof of the officer's seal and signature (s 3(2), (3)), Constitution oaths
-- (s 3(4)), consular fees (ss 4-6), the offences and penalty (ss 7, 8), acts done before 6 January 1969 (s 9), and prosecution
-- (ss 10, 11). The definitions in s 2 are used throughout.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/DCOOFA1968.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates
-- all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; its meta record calls it the
-- current version as at 01 Oct 2026. No later amendment is annotated in the body.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0168 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. The Act is short (11 sections), so the whole of its operative text is encoded. Not encoded: the fees themselves
-- (they are fixed by Ministerial order under s 4, which was not retrieved), the manner of levying and accounting for them (s 4(b)),
-- which countries a President's order under s 3(3) covers, and what "any notarial acts which any notary public can do in Singapore"
-- comprises (that turns on the Notaries Public Act, not read).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Diplomatic and Consular Officers (Oaths and Fees) Act 1968`

§§ `2 -- who is a diplomatic or consular officer`

-- s 2: "consular officer" INCLUDES "any consul general, consul, vice-consul, pro-consul and consular agent of Singapore";
-- "diplomatic officer" INCLUDES "any ambassador, high commissioner, minister, charge d'affaires, deputy high commissioner,
-- secretary and attache of a diplomatic mission of Singapore". Both definitions are inclusive; the list below holds only the named
-- offices, and anyone not named is treated as outside them (an inference -- "includes" does not exclude). The last two entries are
-- not Singapore officers: a member of the foreign service of a Power that represents Singapore's interests (s 3(3)), and a local
-- notary public in the foreign country.
DECLARE Signatory IS ONE OF
    `a Singapore ambassador`
    `a Singapore high commissioner`
    `a charge d'affaires of a Singapore mission`
    `a secretary of a Singapore mission`
    `an attache of a Singapore mission`
    `a Singapore consul general`
    `a Singapore vice-consul`
    `a Singapore consular agent`
    `an officer of a Power representing Singapore`
    `a local notary public abroad`

GIVEN `the signatory` IS A Signatory
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a diplomatic or consular officer of Singapore` IF
    CONSIDER `the signatory`
    WHEN `an officer of a Power representing Singapore` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a local notary public abroad` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `3(1) -- oaths, affidavits and notarial acts abroad`

-- s 3(1): "Every diplomatic officer and consular officer exercising his functions outside Singapore may IN THAT COUNTRY -- (a)
-- administer any oath or affirmation; (b) take any affidavit; and (c) do any notarial acts which any notary public can do in
-- Singapore", and every such act "shall be as effectual as if duly administered, sworn or done by or before any lawful authority in
-- Singapore". s 2: "affidavit" includes any affirmation, statutory or other declaration, acknowledgment, examination, and
-- attestation or protestation of honour.
GIVEN `the signatory` IS A Signatory, `exercising functions outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `done in the country of posting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is as effectual as if done in Singapore` IF
        `is a diplomatic or consular officer of Singapore` `the signatory`
    AND `exercising functions outside Singapore`
    AND `done in the country of posting`

-- s 3(4): for s 3, "oath" includes an oath required for the purposes of the Constitution "provided that such oath is taken before a
-- diplomatic officer or consular officer who is himself a citizen of Singapore".
GIVEN `a Constitution oath` IS A BOOLEAN, `the officer is a Singapore citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may administer the oath` IF
    (NOT `a Constitution oath`) OR `the officer is a Singapore citizen`

§§ `3(2), (3) -- proof of the seal and signature`

-- s 3(2): a document "purporting to have affixed, impressed or subscribed thereon or thereto the SEAL AND SIGNATURE" of a person
-- authorised by s 3 "shall be admitted in evidence without proof of the seal or signature ... or of the official character of that
-- person".
-- s 3(3): the President may by order extend s 3(2), "so much ... as relates to the proof of NOTARIAL ACTS", to persons specified in
-- the order who serve in the foreign service of a Power which, by arrangement, "has undertaken to represent the interests of
-- Singapore in any country or place in which Singapore has no diplomatic or consular representatives".
GIVEN `the signatory` IS A Signatory, `bears the seal and the signature` IS A BOOLEAN, `it attests a notarial act` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the person is specified in a President's order` IS A BOOLEAN, `Singapore has no representatives there` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the document is admitted without proof of seal or signature` IF
        `bears the seal and the signature`
    AND (    `is a diplomatic or consular officer of Singapore` `the signatory`
         OR (    `the signatory` EQUALS `an officer of a Power representing Singapore`
             AND `it attests a notarial act`
             AND `the person is specified in a President's order`
             AND `Singapore has no representatives there`))

§§ `4, 5, 6 -- consular fees`

-- s 4: the Minister may by order in the Gazette "(a) fix the fees to be taken in respect of any matter or thing done in the
-- execution of his office by a diplomatic officer or consular officer entrusted with consular duties".
-- s 6(1): "Subject to any order made under section 4", such an officer "shall not ask for or take any fee or reward for or on
-- account of any act, thing or service done, performed or rendered by him in the execution of his office". (2): contravention is
-- an offence "without prejudice to any other liability".
-- That a fee above the amount fixed is outside the order is an INFERENCE; the Act says only "subject to any order". The amounts are
-- in dollars for the test only; the order states the real currency and figures.
GIVEN `fee asked` IS A NUMBER, `an order fixes a fee for this service` IS A BOOLEAN, `the fixed fee` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the fee may be taken` IF
        `fee asked` AT MOST 0
    OR  (`an order fixes a fee for this service` AND `fee asked` AT MOST `the fixed fee`)

GIVEN `fee asked` IS A NUMBER, `an order fixes a fee for this service` IS A BOOLEAN, `the fixed fee` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `asking for the fee is an offence under s 6` IF
    NOT `the fee may be taken` `fee asked` `an order fixes a fee for this service` `the fixed fee`

-- s 5: every such officer "shall EXHIBIT any subsisting order under section 4 PROMINENTLY in his office and shall PERMIT such order to
-- be inspected by any person wishing to do so at any reasonable time". The Act attaches no offence to s 5 (see s 7 below).
GIVEN `entrusted with consular duties` IS A BOOLEAN, `a subsisting fee order exists` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `exhibited prominently` IS A BOOLEAN, `allowed inspection at a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer complies with s 5` IF
        (NOT `entrusted with consular duties`)
    OR  (NOT `a subsisting fee order exists`)
    OR  (`exhibited prominently` AND `allowed inspection at a reasonable time`)

§§ `6(2), 7 -- offences`

-- s 7: any person who "(a) swears falsely in any oath or affidavit taken or made in accordance with the provisions of this Act; (b)
-- forges or fraudulently alters the seal or signature of any person authorised ... to administer an oath; or (c) tenders in evidence
-- or otherwise uses any affidavit having any seal or signature so forged or counterfeited or fraudulently altered, KNOWING the same
-- to be forged ..." is guilty of an offence. s 6(2) adds the improper fee. s 2: "swear" includes affirm, declare and protest.
DECLARE Conduct IS ONE OF
    `swearing falsely in an oath taken under the Act`
    `affirming falsely in a declaration taken under the Act`
    `forging an officer's seal or signature`
    `fraudulently altering an officer's seal or signature`
    `using a forged affidavit knowing it is forged`
    `using a forged affidavit not knowing it is forged`
    `an officer asking for an unauthorised fee`
    `an officer failing to exhibit the fee order`
    `an officer refusing inspection of the fee order`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an offence under the Act` IF
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `using a forged affidavit not knowing it is forged` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an officer failing to exhibit the fee order` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an officer refusing inspection of the fee order` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `8 -- penalty`

-- s 8: "Any person who is guilty of an offence shall be liable on conviction to a fine NOT EXCEEDING $5,000 or to imprisonment for a
-- term NOT EXCEEDING 3 YEARS or to both." One penalty for every offence, the officer's improper fee included.
`the maximum fine` MEANS 5000

`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS 36

GIVEN `fine imposed` IS A NUMBER, `months imposed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sentence is within s 8` IF
        `fine imposed` AT MOST `the maximum fine`
    AND `months imposed` AT MOST `the maximum imprisonment in months`

§§ `9 -- acts before 6 January 1969`

-- s 9: any oath, affirmation, affidavit and notarial act "administered, sworn or done by any diplomatic officer or consular officer
-- exercising his functions in any country or place outside Singapore PRIOR TO 6 JANUARY 1969 shall be deemed" done under this Act.
-- Dates are written as yyyymmdd numbers.
GIVEN `date of the act` IS A NUMBER, `by an officer exercising functions abroad` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 9 saving applies` IF
    `by an officer exercising functions abroad` AND `date of the act` LESS THAN 19690106

§§ `10, 11 -- prosecution`

-- s 10: "No prosecution shall be instituted in respect of any offence under this Act without the consent of the Public Prosecutor."
-- s 11: any offence may, subject to s 10, "be inquired into, dealt with, tried and punished in Singapore in the same manner and to
-- the same extent AS IF THE OFFENCE HAD BEEN COMMITTED IN SINGAPORE". Where the conduct happened therefore does not matter.
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct, `committed outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Public Prosecutor consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be prosecuted in Singapore` IF
    `is an offence under the Act` `the conduct` AND `the Public Prosecutor consents`
